{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California application screening fee cap","requirement":"A landlord or agent may not charge an application screening fee above the actual out-of-pocket cost of gathering information about the applicant, and in no case more than $30 per applicant; the $30 cap may be adjusted annually for CPI.","key_value":"$30 per applicant, CPI-adjusted annually from January 1, 1998","coverage_conditions":"Applicants who request to rent a residential property; charge may be made when a landlord or agent receives a rental request. Applies to landlords (owners of residential rental property) and their agents.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental applicants; no unit-count or building-age limits stated"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"In no case shall the amount of the application screening fee charged by the landlord or their agent be greater than thirty dollars ($30) per applicant. The thirty dollar ($30) application screening fee may be adjusted annually by the landlord or their agent commensurate with an increase in the Consumer Price Index, beginning on January 1, 1998.","interaction":"Not intended to preempt federal or state housing assistance program provisions governing collection of deposits and fees.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Screening fee refund deadlines and charging conditions","requirement":"A landlord may charge a screening fee only if a compliant screening process is offered, and must not charge when no unit is available or will be available within a reasonable time. Where the full-refund process is used, unselected applicants get the entire fee back within 7 or 30 days.","key_value":"refund within 7 days of selecting a tenant or 30 days of application, whichever first","coverage_conditions":"Applicants for residential rental property who pay or are asked to pay an application screening fee.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental applicants"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"An application screening process in which the landlord or their agent returns the entire screening fee to any applicant who is not selected for tenancy, regardless of the reason, within 7 days of selecting an applicant for tenancy or 30 days of when the application was submitted, whichever occurs first.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.92,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Itemized receipt for application screening fee","requirement":"A landlord or agent must personally, by mail, or by agreed email give the applicant a receipt for the screening fee that itemizes the out-of-pocket expenses and time spent obtaining and processing information about the applicant.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applicants who have paid an application screening fee to a landlord or their agent for a residential rental.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental applicants"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"The landlord or their agent shall provide, personally, or by mail, the applicant with a receipt for the fee paid by the applicant, which receipt shall itemize the out-of-pocket expenses and time spent by the landlord or their agent to obtain and process the information about the applicant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.93,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Order-of-application screening process","requirement":"Where this screening process is used, a landlord must consider completed applications in the order received under written screening criteria, and must approve the first applicant who meets those criteria; criteria must be given to the applicant in writing with the application form.","key_value":"first qualified applicant approved; applications considered in order received","coverage_conditions":"Applicants for residential rental property where the landlord or agent uses the ordered application screening process and charges a screening fee.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental applicants"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"(i) Completed applications are considered, as provided for in the landlord’s established screening criteria, in the order in which the completed applications were received. The landlord’s screening criteria shall be provided to the applicant in writing together with the application form.\n(ii) The first applicant who meets the landlord’s established screening criteria is approved for tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.93,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
